For unit structs, this PR causes the generated code to be slightly worse. For example:

```rust
#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]
pub struct Thing;
```

Relevant generated code on nightly:

```rust
#[automatically_derived]
impl ::core::cmp::PartialOrd for Thing {
    #[inline]
    fn partial_cmp(
        &self,
        other: &Thing,
    ) -> ::core::option::Option<::core::cmp::Ordering> {
        ::core::option::Option::Some(::core::cmp::Ordering::Equal)
    }
}
```

Relevant generated code with this PR:

```rust
#[automatically_derived]
impl ::core::cmp::PartialOrd for Thing {
    #[inline]
    fn partial_cmp(
        &self,
        other: &Thing,
    ) -> ::core::option::Option<::core::cmp::Ordering> {
        ::core::option::Option::Some(self.cmp(other))
