}

struct LocalModuleData {
  kind: LocalModuleDataKind,
  // parent, resolutions, underscore_disambiguator, unexpanded_invocations, globs
}

enum LocalModuleDataKind {
  NonBlock(NonBlockLocalModuleData),
  Block,
}

struct NonBlockLocalModuleData {
  // def_id, node_id, name, glob_importers
}
```

What I want to ideally achieve is to have a set of "smart pointers" `Module`/`LocalModule`/`ExternModule` (newtypes around `Interned<(Local,Extern)ModuleData>`) that would deref both to the shared data and to their specific fields, but without going through 1 or 2 `match`es.
