Hi @asder8215 - great work on this redesign. I have a small complementary optimization: a byte-comparison fast path for `Path::eq`:

```rust
fn eq(&self, other: &Path) -> bool {
    // Byte-identical paths have identical component sequences by definition;
    // this avoids the component-by-component traversal for the common case of
    // looking up the same path in a hash map or deduplication set.
    self.as_os_str() == other.as_os_str() || self.components() == other.components()
}
```

My standalone benchmarks show ~58% improvement on the identical-path case and essentially no regression on different-length paths (the fast path fails instantly on length mismatch). There is a ~7% overhead on same-length-but-different-content paths due to the extra byte scan before falling through to component comparison.

This change is orthogonal to the `Components` redesign — it skips the component traversal entirely for identical paths, while your redesign makes that traversal cheaper for non-identical paths. The two would compose well.

I have an open PR (#158895) for this if you'd like to reference or incorporate it. Happy to contribute it directly here if that's preferred.

